WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.870
First Night It was a beautiful night, the

2
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.830
kind of night that only feels possible when

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.070
we are young, dear reader.

4
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.750
The sky was full of stars, so bright

5
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.690
and endless that, as I looked at it,

6
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.190
I couldn't help but wonder how grumpy or

7
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:19.330
moody people could live under such a sky.

8
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.430
That's a very youthful thought too, dear reader,

9
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:23.610
so youthful.

10
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.050
But may God grant that such thoughts enter

11
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.310
your heart more often.

12
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.650
Speaking of grumpy and moody people, I can't

13
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.270
help but think about how I felt all

14
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:33.550
day.

15
00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.030
From the moment I woke up a strange

16
00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.450
sadness weighed on me.

17
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.630
I couldn't shake the feeling that I was

18
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:42.970
completely alone, that everyone was leaving me behind.

19
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.990
Of course, you might ask, who is this

20
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.550
everyone you're talking about?

21
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.290
After all, I had lived in Petersburg for

22
00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.610
almost eight years and barely knew anyone.

23
00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.170
But what did I need acquaintances for?

24
00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.390
I already felt like I knew all of

25
00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:57.730
Petersburg.

26
00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:01.070
That's why, when everyone in Petersburg seemed to

27
00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.209
pack their things and move to their summer

28
00:01:03.209 --> 00:01:05.650
homes, it felt like they were all leaving

29
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:05.950
me.

30
00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:08.890
The thought of being left behind scared me,

31
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.710
and for three whole days I wandered the

32
00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:14.030
city feeling down, unsure of what to do

33
00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:14.670
with myself.

34
00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.370
Whether I walked along Nevsky Prospekt, visited the

35
00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.910
gardens, or strolled by the river bank, I

36
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.830
didn't see a single familiar face.

37
00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.470
Those people didn't know me, of course, but

38
00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.250
I knew them.

39
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.930
I knew them so well that it felt

40
00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:30.390
like I had studied their faces.

41
00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.870
Their happiness made me happy, and their gloom

42
00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:34.690
brought me down.

43
00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.010
I even felt as though I had formed

44
00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.770
a sort of bond with one old man

45
00:01:38.770 --> 00:01:41.190
I saw every single day at the same

46
00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.270
time on Fontanka.

47
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:46.470
He had a serious, thoughtful expression, and he

48
00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:48.850
always mumbled to himself while waving his left

49
00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:49.170
hand.

50
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.110
In his right hand he carried a long,

51
00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.130
knobby stick with a gold handle.

52
00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.050
He even seemed to notice me and care

53
00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.330
about me in his own way.

54
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.710
If I wasn't at my usual spot on

55
00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.230
Fontanka, I was sure he felt disappointed.

56
00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.490
Over time we almost started nodding to each

57
00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:08.910
other in greeting, especially when we were both

58
00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:09.750
in good spirits.

59
00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.610
Just the other day, after missing each other

60
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.810
for two days, we nearly tipped our hats

61
00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:17.210
as we passed, but we caught ourselves just

62
00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.630
in time and simply exchanged curious glances.

63
00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.210
I know the buildings in Petersburg too.

64
00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:24.910
As I walk down the streets, it feels

65
00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.670
like the buildings lean forward, peeking out their

66
00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:28.770
windows to greet me.

67
00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.730
Some of them seem to say, Good morning.

68
00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:33.530
How are you?

69
00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.250
I'm doing well, thank you, and I'll be

70
00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.890
getting a new floor added in May.

71
00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.450
Others might say, I'm being repainted tomorrow, or

72
00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.130
I narrowly escaped a fire and was so

73
00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:45.530
frightened.

74
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.210
I even have favorites among the buildings.

75
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.350
Some of them feel like old friends.

76
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.590
One building plans to undergo some renovations by

77
00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.610
the architect this summer, and I'll make a

78
00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.570
point of visiting daily to ensure the work

79
00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.170
goes well.

80
00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.630
Heaven forbid anything goes wrong.

81
00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.510
But I'll never forget what happened with a

82
00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.090
small, charming house that used to be a

83
00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.290
lovely shade of pink.

84
00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.250
It was such a delightful little brick house.

85
00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.750
It stood proudly among its plain neighbors, and

86
00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.530
seeing it always lifted my spirits.

87
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.450
Then one day last week I passed by,

88
00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:20.430
and it seemed to cry out to me,

89
00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.370
They're painting me yellow!

90
00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.350
I was horrified.

91
00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:25.970
Those barbarians!

92
00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.030
They didn't spare a single detail, not the

93
00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.710
columns, not the cornices.

94
00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.690
My poor little friend was as yellow as

95
00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:34.270
a canary.

96
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.250
It made me feel sick.

97
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.330
Even now I can't bring myself to visit

98
00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.150
that house, now ruined by its awful new

99
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:42.550
color.

100
00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.950
So now you understand, dear reader, how I

101
00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.610
feel connected to all of Petersburg.

102
00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.630
I already mentioned that I had been feeling

103
00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.970
uneasy for three whole days before I finally

104
00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.650
realized what was bothering me.

105
00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.410
I felt restless on the streets.

106
00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.230
This person was gone.

107
00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.030
That one was gone.

108
00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:02.970
And what had happened to the other?

109
00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.750
Even at home I didn't feel like myself.

110
00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.370
For two nights I racked my brain trying

111
00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.970
to figure out what was wrong in my

112
00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:10.550
little corner.

113
00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.890
Why was it so uncomfortable all of a

114
00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:13.130
sudden?

115
00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.709
In my confusion I carefully inspected the dingy

116
00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:19.870
green walls, the ceiling covered in cobwebs that

117
00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.430
Matrona had allowed to flourish, and all my

118
00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:22.870
furniture.

119
00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.930
I checked every chair, wondering if the issue

120
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.630
was with them, because if even one chair

121
00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.150
isn't in the same spot as the day

122
00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.950
before, I feel unsettled.

123
00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.390
I even studied the window, but none of

124
00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:35.830
it helped.

125
00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.430
Nothing felt better.

126
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.870
I thought about calling Matrona to talk about

127
00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:43.790
the cobwebs and her general carelessness, but when

128
00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:45.990
I finally did, she just stared at me

129
00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:49.450
in silence, clearly baffled, and left without saying

130
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:49.990
a word.

131
00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.790
The cobwebs, of course, are still hanging there,

132
00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:53.570
undisturbed.

133
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.530
It wasn't until this morning that I finally

134
00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.390
figured it out.

135
00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.330
Ah, everyone is leaving for their summer homes.

136
00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.670
Excuse the simplicity of my words, but I'm

137
00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.610
not in the mood for fancy language right

138
00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:05.890
now.

139
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.270
Everything and everyone in Petersburg had either left

140
00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.390
or was preparing to leave for the holidays.

141
00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.070
Every respectable-looking gentleman I saw taking a

142
00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.630
cab seemed to transform in my mind into

143
00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.810
a devoted head of the household on his

144
00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.430
way to join his family at a summer

145
00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:21.690
villa.

146
00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.770
Every passerby seemed to carry an air of

147
00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:26.790
transition, as if to say to the world,

148
00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.410
I'm only here for a little while longer,

149
00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.710
and soon I'll be off to the summer

150
00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:31.970
villa.

151
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.850
If a window opened and a pair of

152
00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.430
delicate snow-white fingers tapped on the glass,

153
00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.050
before a pretty young woman leaned out to

154
00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.850
call to a flower-seller, I immediately imagined

155
00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.150
the flowers weren't for her stuffy apartment, but

156
00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.230
for the countryside, where she would soon be

157
00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:47.570
moving.

158
00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.770
I became so caught up in my new

159
00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:51.790
obsession that I began to feel I could

160
00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.370
tell, just by looking at people, which summer

161
00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.890
villa they were heading to.

162
00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.670
Those going to Kameny or Aptokarsky Islands or

163
00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:02.190
the Peterhof Road stood out with their polished

164
00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.710
manners, stylish summer outfits, and elegant carriages.

165
00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.510
Those bound for Pargolovo or more distant places

166
00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.590
had a calm and dignified air.

167
00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.750
Meanwhile, people heading to Krestovsky Island were unmistakable

168
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.750
with their carefree, lively energy.

169
00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.210
If I happened to see a long line

170
00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:24.830
of carts carrying heaps of furniture—tables, chairs, sofas,

171
00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:28.290
and all sorts of household items—often with an

172
00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.290
old cook perched on top of it all,

173
00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:34.010
fiercely guarding her employer's belongings, or boats loaded

174
00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:37.010
with goods slowly gliding along the Neva or

175
00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.530
Fontanka on their way to the Black River

176
00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:41.950
or the Islands, it felt as though these

177
00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:42.990
scenes were everywhere.

178
00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.170
In my mind I multiplied these wagons and

179
00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.670
boats tenfold, a hundredfold.

180
00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:51.330
It seemed like the whole city was moving

181
00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.130
in caravans to summer villas.

182
00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.630
It felt as if Petersburg was on the

183
00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.250
verge of becoming a ghost town.

184
00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:01.350
I started to feel embarrassed, frustrated, and deeply

185
00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.050
sad that I had no place to go

186
00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.410
for the holidays and no reason to leave

187
00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:05.870
the city.

188
00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:09.410
I wanted to join every wagon, ride off

189
00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:12.130
with every dignified gentleman in a cab, but

190
00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:15.350
no one, not a single person, invited me.

191
00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.430
It was as if they had all forgotten

192
00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.870
about me entirely, as if I didn't belong

193
00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.250
to their world at all.

194
00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.810
I went on long walks, often so lost

195
00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.710
in thought that I forgot where I was

196
00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.050
until I suddenly found myself at the city

197
00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:29.470
gates.

198
00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.950
As soon as I realized where I was,

199
00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:33.950
I felt a wave of relief.

200
00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.990
I crossed the boundary and walked through fields

201
00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:37.510
and meadows.

202
00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.110
I didn't feel tired at all, only as

203
00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.950
though a heavy weight had been lifted from

204
00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:42.430
my heart.

205
00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.250
Everyone I passed looked at me with such

206
00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.710
kind expressions that it felt like they were

207
00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.030
silently greeting me.

208
00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:52.410
They all seemed so cheerful, as if something

209
00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.850
wonderful had just happened, and nearly all of

210
00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:55.990
them were smoking cigars.

211
00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.190
Their happiness made me feel a joy I

212
00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:00.170
hadn't known before.

213
00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:02.210
It felt almost as if I had been

214
00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.270
transported to Italy.

215
00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.970
So powerful was the effect of nature on

216
00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.690
someone like me, a half-sick city dweller,

217
00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.030
suffocating within the walls of the town.

218
00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.050
There is something incredibly moving about the nature

219
00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:15.970
around Petersburg.

220
00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:19.490
Especially in early spring, when it seems to

221
00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.630
use every ounce of strength it has.

222
00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.570
It bursts into bloom, covers itself in green

223
00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.570
leaves, and sprinkles itself with flowers, as if

224
00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.210
putting on its finest attire.

225
00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.770
It reminds me of a delicate, sickly girl,

226
00:08:34.309 --> 00:08:35.909
the kind you might look at with pity

227
00:08:35.909 --> 00:08:39.010
or tenderness, or perhaps not notice at all.

228
00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:44.010
Then, out of nowhere, she becomes breathtakingly beautiful,

229
00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:46.010
almost as if by accident.

230
00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:50.030
Her sad, thoughtful eyes suddenly glow with fire,

231
00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.990
her pale cheeks flush with color, her features

232
00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.870
soften, and her face fills with passion and

233
00:08:56.870 --> 00:08:57.210
life.

234
00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:01.450
Her smile becomes radiant, her laughter sparkles, and

235
00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.190
her beauty overwhelms you.

236
00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.270
It's impossible not to wonder what caused this

237
00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:06.910
transformation.

238
00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:10.590
What gave her such vitality, such life?

239
00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.670
What brought that glow to her face and

240
00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.710
made her movements so full of grace?

241
00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:17.890
But then the moment vanishes.

242
00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.690
The next day you might see her again,

243
00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.670
but she's back to the way she was

244
00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:27.570
before, quiet, pale, and distant, with a look

245
00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:28.990
of sorrow in her eyes.

246
00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.270
You can even sense regret or anguish in

247
00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:34.710
her expression, as if she's mourning the brief,

248
00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.110
fleeting moment of beauty she allowed herself.

249
00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.970
And you feel sad too, heartbroken that her

250
00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:44.090
beauty disappeared so quickly, that it came and

251
00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:45.510
went like a passing dream.

252
00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.350
You grieve because it felt like you didn't

253
00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.550
even have enough time to fully appreciate it,

254
00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:52.230
to truly love her.

255
00:09:52.950 --> 00:09:55.590
And yet, as beautiful as that day was,

256
00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.230
the night that followed was even better.

257
00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.430
Here's what happened.

258
00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.390
I returned to the city very late, and

259
00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.070
it was already ten o'clock by the

260
00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.710
time I was heading back to my lodging.

261
00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.790
My path took me along the canal embankment,

262
00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.530
a place where, at that hour, you never

263
00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:13.710
see a single person.

264
00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:15.930
To be fair, I live in a very

265
00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.310
isolated part of the city.

266
00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.650
I walked along, humming a song.

267
00:10:20.330 --> 00:10:22.750
When I'm happy, I always hum to myself,

268
00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:25.290
like anyone who's joyful but has no one

269
00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.670
to share that happiness with.

270
00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:31.110
Then, out of nowhere, something completely unexpected happened.

271
00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.110
Leaning against the canal railing stood a woman,

272
00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:36.550
her elbows resting on the rail, as she

273
00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:38.950
stared intently at the murky water below.

274
00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.970
She wore a lovely yellow hat and a

275
00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:43.230
stylish black shawl.

276
00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:46.510
She's young, and I bet she has dark

277
00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.550
hair, I thought.

278
00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.270
She didn't seem to notice the sound of

279
00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:52.610
my footsteps or react in any way as

280
00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:55.410
I walked past her, my heart pounding loudly

281
00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:56.210
in my chest.

282
00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:58.490
How odd, I thought.

283
00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:00.650
She must be lost in her thoughts.

284
00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:04.610
Then, suddenly, I stopped in my tracks, frozen.

285
00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:07.650
I heard a soft, muffled sob.

286
00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.070
Yes, there was no mistaking it.

287
00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.490
The woman was crying.

288
00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:15.250
A moment later, the quiet sobs became louder,

289
00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.730
one after another.

290
00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:18.330
My heart sank.

291
00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.550
Though I was usually nervous around women, this

292
00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:22.170
was different.

293
00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:24.510
It felt like an extraordinary moment.

294
00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:27.270
I turned back, took a step toward her,

295
00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:30.470
and was just about to say, Miss, but

296
00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:33.930
stopped myself, realizing how cliché it sounded, like

297
00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:36.050
something out of every Russian novel I'd ever

298
00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:36.370
read.

299
00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.190
That thought alone made me hesitate.

300
00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:41.810
As I fumbled for the right words, she

301
00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:42.950
seemed to collect herself.

302
00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:46.190
She turned her head slightly, noticed me, started,

303
00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:47.790
and quickly looked down.

304
00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.930
Without a word, she moved past me and

305
00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.670
began walking along the embankment.

306
00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:54.790
Instinctively, I followed her.

307
00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:57.410
She must have realized it because she veered

308
00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:00.690
off the embankment, crossed the street, and continued

309
00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:01.570
along the pavement.

310
00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:04.870
I didn't dare cross after her, my heart

311
00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.050
beating wildly like a trapped bird.

312
00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:10.530
Then fate seemed to step in and offer

313
00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.270
me a chance.

314
00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:13.870
On the same side of the pavement where

315
00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.410
she was walking, a man suddenly appeared.

316
00:12:17.050 --> 00:12:19.070
He was wearing evening clothes and looked to

317
00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:21.890
be middle-aged, though his unsteady gait and

318
00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:23.650
the way he leaned against the wall made

319
00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.330
him seem less than dignified.

320
00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:28.570
The woman quickened her pace, walking with the

321
00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.810
nervous urgency you see in women who want

322
00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.430
to avoid being approached at night.

323
00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.730
It seemed likely the staggering man wouldn't follow

324
00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.530
her, except, unfortunately, he did.

325
00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:42.190
Without any warning, the man sprang forward and

326
00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.970
began chasing her at full speed.

327
00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.250
She ran like the wind, but he was

328
00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.610
catching up, getting closer and closer.

329
00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:51.270
She let out a sharp scream, and in

330
00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.170
that instant I silently thanked the sturdy walking

331
00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:55.970
stick I happened to be carrying in my

332
00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:56.630
right hand.

333
00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:59.770
In a heartbeat I crossed the street, and

334
00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.610
in another the drunken man seemed to understand

335
00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:03.370
the situation.

336
00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:07.630
He noticed my stick, recognized the unspoken thread

337
00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:10.370
it carried, and immediately backed off without saying

338
00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:10.850
a word.

339
00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:13.230
Only when we were far down the road

340
00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.270
did I hear him muttering curses in our

341
00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.750
direction, but his voice was too faint to

342
00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:18.250
make out.

343
00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:20.990
Take my arm, I said to the woman.

344
00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.070
He won't bother us any more.

345
00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:26.610
She hesitated for only a moment before linking

346
00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.270
her trembling arm with mine.

347
00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:31.970
She was still shaking, overwhelmed by fear and

348
00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:32.530
excitement.

349
00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:36.470
Oh, drunken stranger, how I silently thanked you

350
00:13:36.470 --> 00:13:37.150
in that moment!

351
00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.630
I glanced at her out of the corner

352
00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.390
of my eye and saw that she was

353
00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:44.150
even more beautiful than I had guessed, dark

354
00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.850
-haired, just as I'd imagined.

355
00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.290
Her long, dark lashes were still wet with

356
00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.830
tears, though I couldn't tell if they were

357
00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.450
from the terror she had just experienced or

358
00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.430
from whatever had made her cry earlier.

359
00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:59.590
Yet a faint smile was beginning to form

360
00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.270
on her lips.

361
00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.770
She, too, stole a quick glance at me,

362
00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.330
her cheeks turning a soft pink before she

363
00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.310
lowered her gaze again.

364
00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.970
You see, I said gently, why did you

365
00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:11.290
push me away earlier?

366
00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.750
If I'd been there, this never would have

367
00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:14.130
happened.

368
00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.730
But I didn't know you, she replied quietly.

369
00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.770
I thought you might have been like him.

370
00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:21.230
And now?

371
00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:23.410
Do you think you know me better?

372
00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.390
Maybe a little, she said, still looking down.

373
00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:29.470
But why are you shaking?

374
00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.470
Oh, you've guessed it right away, I replied,

375
00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.870
thrilled that this girl was so clever.

376
00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:39.130
Intelligence always goes so well with beauty.

377
00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.990
Yes, from the very first look you figured

378
00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:43.950
me out completely.

379
00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.710
You're right, I'm shy around women.

380
00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.530
I get nervous just like you did a

381
00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:51.370
moment ago when that man scared you.

382
00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.310
To be honest, I'm a little nervous now.

383
00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.070
This feels like a dream.

384
00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.230
And I never imagined, even in my wildest

385
00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.150
dreams, that I'd ever have a real conversation

386
00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:02.710
with a woman.

387
00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:03.750
What?

388
00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:04.430
Really?

389
00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.630
Yes, really.

390
00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.630
If my arm is trembling, it's because it

391
00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:11.550
has never been held by a small, lovely

392
00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.250
hand like yours before.

393
00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:15.850
I've never had much to do with women.

394
00:15:16.510 --> 00:15:17.910
You see, I'm always alone.

395
00:15:18.490 --> 00:15:20.010
I don't even know how to talk to

396
00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:20.550
them properly.

397
00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:22.570
In fact, I'm not sure if I've already

398
00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:23.950
said something foolish to you.

399
00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.430
Be honest with me.

400
00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:26.930
Please tell me if I have.

401
00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:28.790
I promise I won't be offended.

402
00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:30.970
No, no, not at all.

403
00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:31.830
Quite the opposite.

404
00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:33.950
And if you really want me to be

405
00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.730
honest, I'll tell you that women actually like

406
00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:37.890
that kind of nervousness.

407
00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:41.250
And to be even more honest, I like

408
00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:41.670
it too.

409
00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.770
I won't send you away until I've made

410
00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:45.530
it home safely.

411
00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.490
You're going to make me lose all my

412
00:15:48.490 --> 00:15:51.370
shyness, I said, almost breathless with happiness.

413
00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:54.490
And once that happens, all my chances will

414
00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:54.970
be gone.

415
00:15:56.110 --> 00:15:56.630
Chances?

416
00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:57.750
What chances?

417
00:15:58.350 --> 00:15:59.970
That's not a very nice thing to say.

418
00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.450
I'm sorry it just slipped out, but how

419
00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:04.930
can anyone not want to make a good

420
00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.510
impression at a moment like this?

421
00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:08.850
You mean to be liked, right?

422
00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:10.810
Yes, exactly.

423
00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.030
But please be kind to me.

424
00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:14.770
Think about who I am.

425
00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.670
I'm twenty-six years old, and I've never

426
00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:18.770
known anyone like you.

427
00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.370
How can I possibly say the right things

428
00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.750
or be smooth and confident?

429
00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:25.570
Maybe you'll understand better if I just tell

430
00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:26.110
you everything.

431
00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.530
I don't know how to keep quiet when

432
00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:31.090
my heart is speaking, but never mind all

433
00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:31.430
that.

434
00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:33.990
Believe me, I've never been with a woman,

435
00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.210
not even once.

436
00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.990
No friendships, no relationships, nothing.

437
00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.290
Every day I just dream about finally meeting

438
00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:42.710
someone.

439
00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.550
Oh, if only you knew how many times

440
00:16:45.550 --> 00:16:47.250
I've fallen in love in my dreams.

441
00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.170
Really?

442
00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.090
With who?

443
00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.770
With no one in particular, with an ideal,

444
00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:56.170
with a person I imagine in my dreams.

445
00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:58.750
I make up entire stories in my head.

446
00:16:59.070 --> 00:17:00.410
You don't know me at all.

447
00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.170
Of course, I've met a few women before,

448
00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.150
but what kind of women were they?

449
00:17:05.829 --> 00:17:09.310
They were all landladies, people like that, but

450
00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.890
I'm sure you'll laugh if I tell you

451
00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:11.190
this.

452
00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.210
I've even thought about speaking to some elegant

453
00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.810
woman on the street a few times.

454
00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:18.490
Of course, only if she was alone.

455
00:17:19.569 --> 00:17:22.650
I imagined myself approaching her timidly and respectfully,

456
00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:25.770
explaining how lonely I am, begging her not

457
00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.730
to turn me away.

458
00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:29.150
I'd tell her that I don't have any

459
00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.710
opportunities to meet women, and that it's almost

460
00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.710
a moral duty for her not to reject

461
00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:35.110
such a desperate request.

462
00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:36.910
I'd ask her to say just a few

463
00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.790
kind words to me, as if she were

464
00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:39.350
my sister.

465
00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:42.350
I wouldn't ask for much, just two or

466
00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:43.550
three words of sympathy.

467
00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:45.770
She could laugh at me if she wanted

468
00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:48.350
to, but I'd hope she wouldn't reject me

469
00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:48.810
outright.

470
00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:51.430
Even if we never saw each other again,

471
00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:53.830
just those few words would mean so much.

472
00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:57.590
But you're laughing now, and that's exactly why

473
00:17:57.590 --> 00:17:58.730
I'm telling you all this.

474
00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:00.790
Don't be upset.

475
00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.230
I'm only laughing at how you're your own

476
00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:03.930
worst enemy.

477
00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:06.690
If you had tried, you might have succeeded,

478
00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:08.650
even if it had been on the street.

479
00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:10.670
Simplicity is best.

480
00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:13.950
No kind-hearted woman, unless she were either

481
00:18:13.950 --> 00:18:15.630
foolish or in a bad mood at the

482
00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:18.090
time, could turn you away without those two

483
00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:20.430
little words you're so shy to ask for.

484
00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.990
But wait, what am I saying?

485
00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:25.410
Of course, she might think you're crazy.

486
00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.190
I was judging by myself.

487
00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.410
I know quite a bit about other people's

488
00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:29.770
lives.

489
00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.430
Oh, thank you, I exclaimed.

490
00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.030
You don't know what you've just done for

491
00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:35.210
me?

492
00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:37.830
I'm glad, I'm so glad.

493
00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.850
But tell me, how did you know I

494
00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:44.310
was the kind of woman who—well, someone you'd

495
00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.290
think worthy—of your attention and friendship?

496
00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:49.670
Not just a landlady, as you say?

497
00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:52.010
What made you decide to approach me?

498
00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.590
What made me?

499
00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:55.370
Well, you were alone.

500
00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.070
That man was being far too rude.

501
00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.890
And it was night-time.

502
00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.870
You have to admit, it felt like my

503
00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:03.150
duty.

504
00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:06.810
No, no, I mean before, when you were

505
00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.230
on the other side of the canal.

506
00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.310
You know you were planning to come up

507
00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:10.570
to me.

508
00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:12.430
The other side?

509
00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.390
Honestly, I don't know how to answer.

510
00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:15.750
I'm afraid to say.

511
00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:17.450
Do you know I've been happy today?

512
00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.170
I walked around singing.

513
00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:20.950
I went out into the countryside.

514
00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:23.690
I've never felt moments like that before.

515
00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.050
You—perhaps I imagined it.

516
00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.770
Forgive me for saying this, but I thought

517
00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:32.010
you were crying, and I couldn't bear it.

518
00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:33.770
It hurt my heart.

519
00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:36.430
Surely it's okay that I was concerned for

520
00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:36.670
you.

521
00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:39.190
Surely there's no harm in feeling a kind

522
00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:41.370
of brotherly compassion for someone?

523
00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:44.170
I'm sorry, I said compassion.

524
00:19:45.230 --> 00:19:47.190
But really, is it wrong for me to

525
00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:49.230
have felt such a strong urge to approach

526
00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:49.470
you?

527
00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.690
Stop, that's enough.

528
00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:54.550
Don't say any more, she said, looking down

529
00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:55.510
and pressing my hand.

530
00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.970
It's my fault for bringing it up.

531
00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.670
But I'm glad I wasn't wrong about you.

532
00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:03.250
And now, here I am at home.

533
00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:05.810
I must turn down this street.

534
00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:08.110
It's just a few steps from here.

535
00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:10.450
Goodbye, and thank you.

536
00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:14.490
Surely, surely you don't mean that we'll never

537
00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:15.470
see each other again?

538
00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.970
This can't be the end, can it?

539
00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:20.910
You see, she said, laughing.

540
00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:23.850
At first, you only wanted two words.

541
00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:27.370
And now—well, I won't say anything.

542
00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:29.230
Maybe we'll meet again.

543
00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:32.190
I'll come here tomorrow, I said.

544
00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:33.450
Oh, forgive me.

545
00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.330
I'm already making demands.

546
00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.230
Yes, you're not very patient.

547
00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:39.690
You're almost insisting.

548
00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:43.670
Listen, please, listen, I interrupted her.

549
00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.450
Forgive me for saying this, but I have

550
00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.470
to tell you something else.

551
00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.170
I can't stop myself from coming back here

552
00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:50.550
tomorrow.

553
00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:51.770
I'm a dreamer.

554
00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:54.750
My real life is so empty that moments

555
00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:56.870
like this are rare treasures for me.

556
00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:59.730
I hold on to them and relive them

557
00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:00.430
in my dreams.

558
00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:03.390
I'll be dreaming of you all night, all

559
00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:04.910
week, maybe all year.

560
00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:08.150
I'll definitely come back here tomorrow, to this

561
00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:10.050
very spot, at the same time.

562
00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:13.730
And I'll feel happy just remembering today.

563
00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:16.190
This place is already special to me.

564
00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.690
I have two or three places like this

565
00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:19.150
in Petersburg.

566
00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:22.730
Once I even cried over memories in one

567
00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:23.450
of those places.

568
00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:25.290
Just like you.

569
00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:28.530
Who knows, maybe ten minutes ago you were

570
00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:30.070
crying over a memory, too.

571
00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:31.450
But forgive me.

572
00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:33.650
I've let myself ramble again.

573
00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:37.170
Perhaps you've been especially happy here once before.

574
00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.810
Very good, said the girl.

575
00:21:40.270 --> 00:21:42.370
Perhaps I will come here tomorrow, too, at

576
00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:42.970
ten o'clock.

577
00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:44.870
I see that I can't forbid you.

578
00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.610
The fact is, I have to be here.

579
00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:50.270
Don't imagine that I'm making an appointment with

580
00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:50.470
you.

581
00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:52.550
I tell you beforehand that I have to

582
00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:53.870
be here on my own account.

583
00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:57.390
But— Well, I tell you straight out, I

584
00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.610
don't mind if you do come.

585
00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.970
To begin with, something unpleasant might happen as

586
00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:03.990
it did today, but never mind that.

587
00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:07.090
In short, I should simply like to see

588
00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:07.310
you.

589
00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:09.410
To say two words to you.

590
00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:11.810
Only mind you must not think the worse

591
00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:12.530
of me now.

592
00:22:13.190 --> 00:22:15.010
Don't think I make appointments so lightly.

593
00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:17.190
I shouldn't make it except that.

594
00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:20.050
But let that be my secret, only a

595
00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:21.230
compact beforehand.

596
00:22:22.170 --> 00:22:23.110
A compact?

597
00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:26.070
Speak, tell me, tell me all beforehand.

598
00:22:26.390 --> 00:22:27.570
I agree to anything.

599
00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:30.610
I am ready for anything, I cry delighted.

600
00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:32.330
I answer for myself.

601
00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:34.670
I will be obedient, respectful.

602
00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:36.050
You know me.

603
00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:39.250
It's just because I do know you that

604
00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:41.370
I ask you to come tomorrow, said the

605
00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:42.050
girl, laughing.

606
00:22:42.810 --> 00:22:44.150
I know you perfectly.

607
00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:47.050
But mind you will come on the condition

608
00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:48.290
in the first place.

609
00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:51.090
Only be good, do what I ask.

610
00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:52.790
You see, I speak frankly.

611
00:22:53.590 --> 00:22:55.270
You won't fall in love with me.

612
00:22:56.190 --> 00:22:58.090
That's impossible, I assure you.

613
00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.430
I am ready for friendship.

614
00:22:59.910 --> 00:23:00.710
Here's my hand.

615
00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:03.330
But you mustn't fall in love with me,

616
00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:04.110
I beg you.

617
00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:07.870
I swear, I cried, gripping her hand.

618
00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:09.950
Hush, don't swear.

619
00:23:10.290 --> 00:23:12.030
I know you are ready to flare up

620
00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:12.930
like gunpowder.

621
00:23:13.630 --> 00:23:15.770
Don't think ill of me for saying so.

622
00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:19.010
If only you knew, I too have no

623
00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:20.390
one to whom I can say a word,

624
00:23:20.790 --> 00:23:22.210
whose advice I can ask.

625
00:23:22.950 --> 00:23:24.750
Of course, one does not look for an

626
00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:26.810
advisor in the street, but you are an

627
00:23:26.810 --> 00:23:27.270
exception.

628
00:23:27.910 --> 00:23:29.250
I know you as though we had been

629
00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:30.570
friends for twenty years.

630
00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:33.150
You won't deceive me, will you?

631
00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:34.850
You will see.

632
00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:38.070
The only thing is, I don't know how

633
00:23:38.070 --> 00:23:39.770
I am going to survive the next twenty

634
00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:40.470
-four hours.

635
00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:45.210
Sleep soundly, good night, and remember that I

636
00:23:45.210 --> 00:23:46.470
have trusted you already.

637
00:23:47.090 --> 00:23:50.350
But you exclaimed so nicely just now, surely

638
00:23:50.350 --> 00:23:53.150
one can't be held responsible for every feeling,

639
00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:55.070
even for brotherly sympathy.

640
00:23:56.150 --> 00:23:58.250
Do you know that was so nicely said,

641
00:23:58.530 --> 00:24:00.830
that the idea struck me at once, that

642
00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:02.110
I might confide in you?

643
00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:05.090
For God's sake do, but about what?

644
00:24:05.350 --> 00:24:05.850
What is it?

645
00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:07.430
Wait till tomorrow.

646
00:24:08.050 --> 00:24:09.450
Meanwhile, let that be a secret.

647
00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:11.350
So much the better for you.

648
00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:13.430
It will give it a faint flavor of

649
00:24:13.430 --> 00:24:13.870
romance.

650
00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:17.050
Perhaps I will tell you tomorrow, and perhaps

651
00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:17.510
not.

652
00:24:18.230 --> 00:24:19.490
I will talk to you a little more

653
00:24:19.490 --> 00:24:19.990
beforehand.

654
00:24:20.690 --> 00:24:22.290
We will get to know each other better.

655
00:24:23.490 --> 00:24:25.390
Oh, yes, I will tell you all about

656
00:24:25.390 --> 00:24:26.250
myself tomorrow.

657
00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:28.130
But what has happened?

658
00:24:28.710 --> 00:24:30.890
It is as though a miracle had befallen

659
00:24:30.890 --> 00:24:31.250
me.

660
00:24:32.410 --> 00:24:34.130
My God, where am I?

661
00:24:34.770 --> 00:24:36.690
Come tell me, aren't you glad that you

662
00:24:36.690 --> 00:24:38.410
were not angry and did not drive me

663
00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:40.430
away at the first moment as any other

664
00:24:40.430 --> 00:24:41.230
woman would have done?

665
00:24:41.650 --> 00:24:43.450
In two minutes you have made me happy

666
00:24:43.450 --> 00:24:43.930
forever.

667
00:24:44.630 --> 00:24:45.390
Yes, happy.

668
00:24:45.830 --> 00:24:48.570
Who knows, perhaps, you have reconciled me with

669
00:24:48.570 --> 00:24:50.650
myself, solved my doubts.

670
00:24:51.770 --> 00:24:53.510
Perhaps such moments come upon me.

671
00:24:54.790 --> 00:24:56.610
But there I will tell you all about

672
00:24:56.610 --> 00:24:57.150
it tomorrow.

673
00:24:57.690 --> 00:24:59.830
You shall know everything, everything.

674
00:25:00.750 --> 00:25:02.190
Very well, I consent.

675
00:25:02.630 --> 00:25:03.370
You shall begin.

676
00:25:04.610 --> 00:25:05.110
Agreed.

677
00:25:05.890 --> 00:25:07.110
Goodbye till tomorrow.

678
00:25:08.110 --> 00:25:09.130
Till tomorrow.

679
00:25:10.330 --> 00:25:11.390
And we parted.

680
00:25:11.870 --> 00:25:13.230
I walked about all night.

681
00:25:13.630 --> 00:25:15.070
I could not make up my mind to

682
00:25:15.070 --> 00:25:15.570
go home.

683
00:25:15.570 --> 00:25:17.050
I was so happy.

684
00:25:17.730 --> 00:25:18.330
Tomorrow.
